{"id":3920,"date":"2021-10-25T13:58:32","date_gmt":"2021-10-25T20:58:32","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=3920"},"modified":"2025-10-23T13:23:39","modified_gmt":"2025-10-23T20:23:39","slug":"1-7-leds-junior-cde-blockly","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/1-7-leds-junior-cde-blockly\/","title":{"rendered":"1.7: LEDs"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22134e6434e\" name=\"6a22134e6434e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>We've Moved!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1761251012580{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-11766\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/icon_warning-150x150-2-84x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"81\" height=\"82\" \/><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><strong>We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: <a href=\"http:\/\/learn.robolink.com\">Robolink Learn<\/a>! Lessons here will remain available until the end of June 2026. This version of Basecamp will no longer be updated and uses outdated references to Blockly for Robolink. You can access the previous version of <a href=\"https:\/\/codrone.robolink.com\/edu\/blockly-archive\/\">Blockly here<\/a>.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22134e6447d\" name=\"6a22134e6447d\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What is an LED?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><strong>LED<\/strong> stands for \u201clight-emitting diode\u201d. A <\/span><b>diode <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">is an electronic device that allows an electronic current to flow in only one direction. LEDs are beginning to replace traditional light bulbs because they are more efficient.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your CoDrone EDU has 2 <\/span><b>RGB <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">LEDs: one in the center of the drone and one in the remote controller. RGB stands for red, green, and blue. Using the three colors, you can create almost every color imaginable! Aside from making your drone look cool, LEDs provide another form of feedback. For example, the drone light can tell you the connection status of your drone. A solid light means your drone is connected, while a fl<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">ashing light indicates there&#8217;s a disconnection.<br \/>\n<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22134e644ed\" name=\"6a22134e644ed\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Parameters<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CoDrone EDU provides functionality so that you can either change the drone&#8217;s LED or the remote controller&#8217;s LED<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">! All of these functions can be found in the &#8220;Lights&#8221; menu.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Each LED block has one or more of these parameters:<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Color &#8211; <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To change the color of the LEDs, click on the color. It will bring up a menu so that you can choose which color you want to change your CoDrone EDU LEDs to.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><strong>Brightness &#8211;<\/strong> In the solid LED blocks, <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">this refers to the<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">light&#8217;s brightness, with 0 being off and 255 being full brightness. <\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12669&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22134e6453f\" name=\"6a22134e6453f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>LED Rainbow<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Pair to CoDrone EDU and practice using the LEDs to make a rainbow. Make sure each color shows for one second before switching to the next color. For optimal brightness, set the brightness to 255. Use the <strong>wait<\/strong> block in between the color blocks so you can see each color before it moves on to the next one. Use a <strong>repeat<\/strong> block to repeat the pattern.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;8989&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22134e645b6\" name=\"6a22134e645b6\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div><strong>Challenge: Disco Drone<\/strong><\/div>\n<div>Program your drone to turn like a disco! Here is your challenge:<\/div>\n<ul>\n<li>Use the <strong>turn degrees<\/strong> block to turn a total of 360 degrees.<\/li>\n<li>The LED on the drone and controller have to change every 90 degrees.<\/li>\n<li>Add a 1-second <strong>wait<\/strong> block before each LED command<\/li>\n<li><em>Hint: <\/em>Alternate turning 90 degrees and changing colors 4 times<\/li>\n<li><em>Bonus:<\/em> Put your disco code in a loop so it repeats 3 times before landing<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22134e6460b\" name=\"6a22134e6460b\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Lesson Complete<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>In this lesson, you learned about the CoDrone EDU\u2019s LEDs. You can control both the drone and the controller LEDs. In the next lesson, you will put it all together to make a remote control.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7547&#8243; img_size=&#8221;750&#215;670&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 7 We've Moved! [vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1761251012580{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}\"] We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: Robolink Learn! Lessons here&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/1-7-leds-junior-cde-blockly\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":4741,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":3877,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1817,1763,1777,1793,626,1533,1438,853,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2135,2108,4328,14401,2120,2122],"class_list":["post-3920","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-beginner","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-cde","lesson-tag-cdej","lesson-tag-led","lesson-tag-programming","module-beginner","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.